# Stray compiler listings: `-o vdi.s` once put one at the root, a
# zero-byte `none` came from a redirect, and `t.s` came from a one-off
# `cc65816 -S` while checking codegen.  All three were committed by
# accident, which is three times, so the rule is now the shape of the
# mistake rather than a list of its instances: a single-letter or
# obviously scratch .s at the ROOT is never a source file -- every real
# one lives in src/.
/vdi.s
/none
/t.s
/?.s
